Changelog: 25-11-2026 17:01:45

Fixed. When GitHub's servers fail during Push, the step now says the fault is GitHub's. It names
"! [remote rejected] ... (fatal error ...)" and HTTP 5xx answers. It said only that the push ended with exit code 1.
githubstatus.com can report such a fault only minutes later, so the GitHub status pill stayed green. When GitHub
refuses a push for another reason, the step shows GitHub's reason.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 20:47:37

Fixed. The tooltip of Record new video now says the recording takes a few minutes, with the voice of Nexus TTS's
speech engine. It said about a minute.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 16:47:44

Added. The Commit step lists the wiki's sections to read again first (tools/check_wiki.py), on the Commands tab, before
the version and manifest checks. The list never stops the commit.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 17:19:51

Fixed. The last two steps changed places (owner, 20-11-2026: git pull could be pressed while jobs still ran, and the tool said finished while git pull was still to press). Step 9 is All runs finished: it waits until GitHub runs nothing more, and git pull stays off until then. Step 10 is Bring in the pin commit, the last thing to press. The line "The release is out and pulled in: ready." (it was "All runs finished, ready.") comes only after that pull.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 16:52:11

Fixed. The Current release box counts the time the steps of the release worked, not the time since the first step was pressed (owner, 20-11-2026: "very bizarre numbers", 48 min 28 s against 3 min 39 s). A window left open between two steps counted as release time: Get up to date at 15:37, the release at 16:27, and the 40 minutes between them were in it. Counted now: a command that runs here (Get up to date, Commit, Push with CI's jobs, Start), GitHub's CI on the commit and the release run, up to the device test. Not counted: the time the tool waits for a step to be pressed, and the time the tool is closed. The times measured before, waiting included, are no longer the Previous release: until a release is timed the new way, that box shows GitHub's own time.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:17:31

Fixed. The time boxes are Previous release, Current release and Deviation (owner, 20-11-2026: "Recorded time is incorrect"; opened for a new release, what is out is the previous one). Previous release is the last release that went out, with the time this tool measured for it, or GitHub's own (its CI and its release run) for one it did not time. Current release is the release being made: its time starts with the first step pressed, runs on this computer's clock and ends when the release on GitHub passed; a dash until a step is pressed. Before, the first box read This release for the release that was out already and counted GitHub's CI and release run only.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:38:39

Added. Start new release starts by itself, without its question, when CI passes on the commit while the window is open and waited for it (owner, 20-11-2026); a window opened on a commit whose CI passed earlier starts nothing by itself, and release/autostart=false in NRT's settings turns it off. A tenth step, All runs finished (owner, 20-11-2026): after Publish and the pin commit it waits while GitHub still runs something (the wiki, the runs on the portal's tag) and names the runs, then reads "All runs finished, ready."; before, every step had its check while a run went on.

Fixed. The release's time counts every step up to the device test (owner, 20-11-2026: "Recorded time is incorrect"): its first part runs from the commit the release started from to the end of GitHub's CI on it, so the push with CI's jobs here is in it; it was GitHub's CI alone, 1 min 39 s where the push took 17 minutes. The three time boxes are wider (240 px at least). The first box reads This release only while that release is being made (its run goes on, or its steps are not done), else Latest release, and the second reads Release before it; during steps 1 to 4 the first box read This release for the release that was out already.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 12:37:04

Added. The Nexus release tab shows how long the release took up to its device test, how long the one before it took, and the deviation between the two (owner, 20-11-2026), in three boxes above the steps. A deviation over 2 minutes also shows in an orange banner; under that, and at 0 or less, the box alone says it. The time is GitHub's: CI on the commit the release started from, and from the release commit to the end of the release on GitHub; the waiting between the two and the steps on this computer are not counted. While the release runs, its time is the time so far. The limit is DEVIATION_LIMIT in flow.py, or release/deviation_limit (seconds) in NRT's settings.

